syntax-head-prefix-op.mo:4.11-4.12: syntax error [M0275], unexpected token '-', expected a block `{ ... }`: `switch` and `do` always take a block, and so do the branches or body of `if`/`while`/`for` when the condition or head is an unparenthesized compound expression (a call, index, projection, or operator application); parenthesize it to keep bare branches — an unspaced `(`/`[` after a bare identifier continues the condition (`if c[i] ...` indexes `c`), a spaced one starts the branch (`if c [i] ...`)
